<title>UK: British-Borneo continues uptrend.</title>
<headline>British-Borneo continues uptrend.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-Borneo Petroleum Syndicate Plc advanced 32-1/2 pence to 1058-1/2, adding to the gains posted last week when the stock was boosted by vague bid talk and positive comments from HSBC James Capel.</p>
<p>Market makers, noting turnover was a mere 119,455 shares, said the same factors were behind the rise today.</p>
<p>But no names of potential bidders were circulating and analysts at HSBC James Capel were unavailable to comment.</p>
<p>British-Borneo, which has promising prospects in the Gulf of Mexico, has been rising non-stop since January 6 when they closed at 802-1/2 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
